insert into public.syllabus_versions (syllabus_id,version,units) select id,1,'[{"title":"Unit","topics":["1. MOS transistor theory and modelling (8 Hours) The Metal Oxide Semiconductor (MOS) Structure MOS System under External Bias Structure and Operation of MOS Transistor (MOSFET) Current-Voltage Characteristics Scaling and Small-geometry Effects MOSFET modelling Small-signal model","The Metal Oxide Semiconductor (MOS) Structure","MOS System under External Bias","Structure and Operation of MOS Transistor (MOSFET)","Current-Voltage Characteristics","Scaling and Small-geometry Effects","MOSFET modelling","Small-signal model","2. Fabrication and Layout of CMOS ICS (8 Hours) Fabrication Process Flow: Basic Steps CMOS Well Process Layout Design Rules Full-Custom Mask Layout Design","Fabrication Process Flow: Basic Steps","CMOS Well Process","Layout Design Rules","Full-Custom Mask Layout Design","3. MOS INVERTERS (10 Hours) Static characteristics: Resistive-Load Inverter, Inverters with n-Type MOSFET Load, CMOS Inverter Switching characteristics and interconnect effects: Delay-Time definitions, Calculation of Delay times, Inverter Design with Delay Constraints Estimation of Interconnect Parasitics, Calculation of Interconnect Delay Switching Power Dissipation of CMOS Inverters","Static characteristics: Resistive-Load Inverter, Inverters with n-Type MOSFET Load, CMOS Inverter","Switching characteristics and interconnect effects: Delay-Time definitions, Calculation of Delay times, Inverter Design with Delay Constraints","Estimation of Interconnect Parasitics, Calculation of Interconnect Delay","Switching Power Dissipation of CMOS Inverters","4. Combinational MOS logic circuits (8 Hours) MOS Logic Circuits with Depletion nMOS Loads CMOS Logic Circuits Complex Logic Circuits CMOS Transmission Gates (Pass Gates)","MOS Logic Circuits with Depletion nMOS Loads","CMOS Logic Circuits","Complex Logic Circuits","CMOS Transmission Gates (Pass Gates)","5. Sequential MOS logic circuits (8 Hours) Behaviour of Bistable elements The SR Latch Circuit Clocked Latch and Flip-Flop Circuits CMOS D-Latch and Edge-Triggered Flip-Flop","Behaviour of Bistable elements","The SR Latch Circuit","Clocked Latch and Flip-Flop Circuits","CMOS D-Latch and Edge-Triggered Flip-Flop","Total: 42 Hours","\"CMOS: Digital Integrated Circuits\", by Sung-Mo Kang and Yusuf Leblibici, 3rd edition, McGraw-Hill Higher Education, 2003","\"CMOS Logic Circuit Design\", by John P. Uyemura, Kluwer Academic Publishers, 2001","\"CMOS VLSI Design: A Circuits and Systems Perspective\", by Neil Weste and David Harris, 4th Edition","\"CMOS: Circuit Design, Layout and Simulation\", by R. Jacob Baker, 3rd edition, IEEE press, 2010"]}]'::jsonb from s;
insert into public.syllabus_versions (syllabus_id,version,units) select id,1,'[{"title":"Unit","topics":["1. Digital Image Fundamentals Elements of visual perception Image sensing and acquisition Image sampling and quantization Basic relationships between pixels – neighborhood, adjacency, connectivity, distance measures","Elements of visual perception","Image sensing and acquisition","Image sampling and quantization","Basic relationships between pixels – neighborhood, adjacency, connectivity, distance measures","2. Image Enhancements and Filtering Gray level transformations Histogram equalization and specifications Pixel-domain smoothing filters – linear and order-statistics Pixel-domain sharpening filters – first and second derivative Two-dimensional DFT and its inverse Frequency domain filters – low-pass and high-pass","Gray level transformations","Histogram equalization and specifications","Pixel-domain smoothing filters – linear and order-statistics","Pixel-domain sharpening filters – first and second derivative","Two-dimensional DFT and its inverse","Frequency domain filters – low-pass and high-pass","3. Color Image Processing Color models–RGB, YUV, HSI Color transformations– formulation, color complements, color slicing, tone and color corrections Color image smoothing and sharpening Color Segmentation","Color models–RGB, YUV, HSI","Color transformations– formulation, color complements, color slicing, tone and color corrections","Color image smoothing and sharpening","Color Segmentation","4. Image Segmentation Detection of discontinuities Edge linking and boundary detection Thresholding– global and adaptive Region-based segmentation","Detection of discontinuities","Edge linking and boundary detection","Thresholding– global and adaptive","Region-based segmentation","5. Wavelets and Multi-resolution image processing Uncertainty principles of Fourier Transform Time frequency localization Continuous wavelet transforms Wavelet bases and multi-resolution analysis Wavelets and Subband filter banks, wavelet packets Image Compression: Redundancy–inter-pixel and psycho-visual; Lossless compression – predictive, entropy; Lossy compression predictive and transform coding; Discrete Cosine Transform; Still image compression standards–JPEG and JPEG-2000","Uncertainty principles of Fourier Transform","Time frequency localization","Continuous wavelet transforms","Wavelet bases and multi-resolution analysis","Wavelets and Subband filter banks, wavelet packets","Image Compression: Redundancy–inter-pixel and psycho-visual; Lossless compression – predictive, entropy; Lossy compression predictive and transform coding; Discrete Cosine Transform; Still image compression standards–JPEG and JPEG-2000","6. Fundamentals of Video Coding Inter-frame redundancy Motion estimation techniques – full-search, fast search strategies, forward and backward motion prediction Frame classification – I, P and B Video sequence hierarchy–Group of pictures, frames, slices, macro-blocks and blocks Elements of a video encoder and decoder Video coding standards – MPEG and H.26X Video Segmentation: Temporal segmentation–shot boundary detection, hard cuts and soft-cuts; spatial segmentation–motion-based; Video object detection and tracking","Inter-frame redundancy","Motion estimation techniques – full-search, fast search strategies, forward and backward motion prediction","Frame classification – I, P and B","Video sequence hierarchy–Group of pictures, frames, slices, macro-blocks and blocks","Elements of a video encoder and decoder","Video coding standards – MPEG and H.26X","Video Segmentation: Temporal segmentation–shot boundary detection, hard cuts and soft-cuts; spatial segmentation–motion-based; Video object detection and tracking","R.C. Gonzalez and R.E. Woods, \"Digital Image Processing\", Second Edition, Pearson Education, 3rd edition 2008","Anil Kumar Jain, \"Fundamentals of Digital Image Processing\", Prentice Hall of India, 2nd edition 2004","Murat Tekalp, \"Digital Video Processing\", Prentice Hall, 2nd edition 2015"]}]'::jsonb from s;
insert into public.syllabus_versions (syllabus_id,version,units) select id,1,'[{"title":"Unit","topics":["1. Introduction Sources of Approximations Data Error and Computational Truncation Error and Rounding Error Absolute Error and Relative Error Sensitivity and Conditioning Backward Error Analysis Stability and Accuracy Computer Arithmetic: Floating Point Numbers, Normalization, Properties of Floating Point System, Rounding, Machine Precision, Subnormal and Gradual Underflow, Exceptional Values, Floating-Point Arithmetic, Cancellation","Sources of Approximations","Data Error and Computational","Truncation Error and Rounding Error","Absolute Error and Relative Error","Sensitivity and Conditioning","Backward Error Analysis","Stability and Accuracy","Computer Arithmetic: Floating Point Numbers, Normalization, Properties of Floating Point System, Rounding, Machine Precision, Subnormal and Gradual Underflow, Exceptional Values, Floating-Point Arithmetic, Cancellation","2. System of Linear Equations Linear Systems, Solving Linear Systems Gaussian elimination, Pivoting, Gauss-Jordan Norms and Condition Numbers Symmetric Positive Definite Systems and Indefinite System Iterative Methods for Linear Systems Linear least squares: Data Fitting, Linear Least Squares, Normal Equations Method, Orthogonalization Methods, QR factorization, Gram-Schmidt Orthogonalization, Rank Deficiency, and Column Pivoting","Linear Systems, Solving Linear Systems","Gaussian elimination, Pivoting, Gauss-Jordan","Norms and Condition Numbers","Symmetric Positive Definite Systems and Indefinite System","Iterative Methods for Linear Systems","Linear least squares: Data Fitting, Linear Least Squares, Normal Equations Method, Orthogonalization Methods, QR factorization, Gram-Schmidt Orthogonalization, Rank Deficiency, and Column Pivoting","3. Eigenvalues, Singular Values, Nonlinear Equations, and Optimization Eigenvalues and singular values: Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors, Methods for Computing All Eigenvalues, Jacobi Method, Methods for Computing Selected Eigenvalues, Singular Values Decomposition, Application of SVD Nonlinear equations: Fixed Point Iteration, Newton''s Method, Inverse Interpolation Method Optimization: One-Dimensional Optimization, Multidimensional Unconstrained Optimization, Nonlinear Least Squares","Eigenvalues and singular values: Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors, Methods for Computing All Eigenvalues, Jacobi Method, Methods for Computing Selected Eigenvalues, Singular Values Decomposition, Application of SVD","Nonlinear equations: Fixed Point Iteration, Newton''s Method, Inverse Interpolation Method","Optimization: One-Dimensional Optimization, Multidimensional Unconstrained Optimization, Nonlinear Least Squares","4. Interpolation, Numerical Integration, and Differential Equations Interpolation: Purpose for Interpolation, Choice of Interpolating Function, Polynomial Interpolation, Piecewise Polynomial Interpolation Numerical Integration And Differentiation: Quadrature Rule, Newton-Cotes Rule, Gaussian Quadrature Rule, Finite Difference Approximation Initial Value Problems for ODEs: Euler''s Method, Taylor Series Method, Runga-Kutta Method, Extrapolation Methods Boundary Value Problems For ODEs: Finite Difference Methods, Finite Element Method, Eigenvalue Problems","Interpolation: Purpose for Interpolation, Choice of Interpolating Function, Polynomial Interpolation, Piecewise Polynomial Interpolation","Numerical Integration And Differentiation: Quadrature Rule, Newton-Cotes Rule, Gaussian Quadrature Rule, Finite Difference Approximation","Initial Value Problems for ODEs: Euler''s Method, Taylor Series Method, Runga-Kutta Method, Extrapolation Methods","Boundary Value Problems For ODEs: Finite Difference Methods, Finite Element Method, Eigenvalue Problems","5. Advanced Topics Partial Differential Equations: Time Dependent Problems, Time Independent Problems, Solution for Sparse Linear Systems, Iterative Methods Fast Fourier Transform: FFT Algorithm, L